                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c76f142-c5af-3f06-919a-6ca20888a797",
                        "entry_id": "3409191e-fc9e-392c-8318-3e0b299c70fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. выкупать; получение чего-либо, удерживаемого до получения оплаты"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dba8b88d-27db-41cf-ba9e-1a54ba1fc619",
                                "sense_id": "5c76f142-c5af-3f06-919a-6ca20888a797",
                                "text": "Ещё в начале февраля 2009 го́да авиакомпания допустила технический дефолт по выкупу дебютных облигаций в размере 2,3 млрд рублей."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1b1ef61-5f7d-3916-b52d-721453a1c292",
                        "entry_id": "3409191e-fc9e-392c-8318-3e0b299c70fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "плата, вносимая для осуществления выкупа [1]"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5bfd8c1-7ee1-4d3e-abaf-f8a182ffa394",
                                "sense_id": "d1b1ef61-5f7d-3916-b52d-721453a1c292",
                                "text": "Джон должен собрать фантастическую сумму в два миллиона фунтов, заплатить выкуп."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c7b1c8e0-bd1e-377d-891d-143d3e7083ed",
                        "entry_id": "3409191e-fc9e-392c-8318-3e0b299c70fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. уплата крестьянами платежей за земельные наделы, предоставленные им реформой 1861 го́да в России"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59394248-3599-4e61-9534-5588a1199f7d",
                                "sense_id": "c7b1c8e0-bd1e-377d-891d-143d3e7083ed",
                                "text": "19 февраля. Сегодня по старому стилю отмечают 150-летие освобождения крестьян. ⟨…⟩ Правда, как у нас принято, многого не договаривают, например, об ограниченности гражданских прав, отсутствии политических свобод, выкупе земли́, временнообязанном положении, сохранении общинных пут и т. д. и т. п."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b77dbc8-6ff7-4269-ab81-df4c319d43d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "3409191e-fc9e-392c-8318-3e0b299c70fb",
                        "source_sense_description": "плата",
                        "target_lang_word": "ransom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ransom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                        "entry_id": "b7b5346c-016e-327a-a1ef-6f15fd3d976a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Money paid for the freeing of a hostage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e93eaee-6ca7-4cca-a908-8352bd67a2ee",
                                                "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                                "text": "They were held for two million dollars ransom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e9aeefe-fb22-4ea5-989a-243d0796b9e1",
                                                "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                                "text": "They were held to ransom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f227d4c-20f1-4dad-b502-38a7ab43b12b",
                                                "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                                "text": "Thy ransom paid, which man from death redeems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bca913c-ef08-4782-87f6-ba95078e7b67",
                                                "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                                "text": "His captivity in Austria, and the heavy ransom he paid for his liberty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee772c8f-1731-4cfc-9206-3d6377d7b44d",
                                                "sense_id": "75fe4a74-e10c-3dcd-85ac-77c45af2d7fa",
                                                "text": "As rich as was the ransom Priam paid for Hektor, Hermes says, his remaining sons at Troy “'would give three times as much ransom / for you, who are alive, were Atreus' son Agamemnon / to recognize you.'”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73dbb52a-c44d-37a3-a381-336d5abe91cd",
                                        "entry_id": "b7b5346c-016e-327a-a1ef-6f15fd3d976a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The release of a captive, or of captured property, by payment of a consideration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3baf597-c6ee-440f-89dc-88a0638ebe8c",
                                                "sense_id": "73dbb52a-c44d-37a3-a381-336d5abe91cd",
                                                "text": "prisoners hopeless of ransom"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34b143fe-1306-403e-8ce0-d2e5e0dbfba4",
                                                "sense_id": "73dbb52a-c44d-37a3-a381-336d5abe91cd",
                                                "text": "Till the fair slave be rendered to her sire; And ransom-free restored to his abode"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "331c7f42-94b2-3ed0-b27c-0fbfeb48a26d",
                                        "entry_id": "b7b5346c-016e-327a-a1ef-6f15fd3d976a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sum paid for the pardon of some great offence and the discharge of the offender; also, a fine paid in lieu of corporal punishment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39eeba32-cecd-4449-8ff1-90e8fa86e6be",
                                                "sense_id": "331c7f42-94b2-3ed0-b27c-0fbfeb48a26d",
                                                "text": "punished with imprisonment and ransom at the King's will"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ransom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67a2c2d3-11f7-30dc-89d9-4be8fcd94e32",
                                        "entry_id": "71d54c39-8cea-37da-8a8c-086b2e438bab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deliver, especially in context of sin or relevant penalties."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9db84f24-e131-3170-b237-5e31ded288e4",
                                        "entry_id": "71d54c39-8cea-37da-8a8c-086b2e438bab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pay a price to set someone free from captivity or punishment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef38c6f8-a3ac-4abb-a0e6-7c9ddf1ec600",
                                                "sense_id": "9db84f24-e131-3170-b237-5e31ded288e4",
                                                "text": "to ransom prisoners from an enemy"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6c02b87-7a51-46e0-a4d2-7ff0767ee142",
                                                "sense_id": "9db84f24-e131-3170-b237-5e31ded288e4",
                                                "text": "And gainſt the General we will lift our ſwords\nAnd either lanch his greedie thirſting throat,\nOr take him priſoner, and his chaine ſhall ſerue\nFor Manackles, till he be ranſom’d home."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fce22f3b-3a73-34da-8430-f192be912ed9",
                                        "entry_id": "71d54c39-8cea-37da-8a8c-086b2e438bab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exact a ransom (payment) in exchange for the freedom of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c98acda7-def2-47dd-b129-4e2d43736a37",
                                                "sense_id": "fce22f3b-3a73-34da-8430-f192be912ed9",
                                                "text": "Terrorists will continue to hold few detainees in undisclosed locations in order to ransom them for money or some other material profit, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
